{"units": [{"id": "mvp-comment-345-3-mentioned1", "translation": "what then"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-comment1", "translation": "On ⟦1⟧ cf. 1008 ⟦2⟧, victory and excelling in everything, except in battles, for victory in ⟦3⟧ (861 ff., 976 ff.) is nothing good. Differently ⟦4⟧ (cowardly) ⟦5⟧. ⟦6⟧ from ⟦7⟧ aim, aiming at, as ⟦8⟧ ⟦9⟧, i.e. ⟦10⟧ according to the scholia, ⟦11⟧ ⟦12⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned1", "translation": "of victory"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned2", "translation": "to send what is profitable to the city for victory"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned3", "translation": "faction, civil strife"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned4", "translation": "evil victory"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned5", "translation": "overseer, guardian"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned6", "translation": "mark, target"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned7", "translation": "aimed at"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-mentioned8", "translation": "to shoot at a mark"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-1-quote1", "translation": "a song that watches over this ruin"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-2-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ as ⟦2⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-2-mentioned1", "translation": "from the earth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-3-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ generally means 'moisture', as ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ of blood; of sea- or river-water ⟦4⟧. 1192 (⟦5⟧, ⟦6⟧), Hippol. 192 (⟦7⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-3-mentioned1", "translation": "dew, moisture"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-3-mentioned2", "translation": "of bloody dew"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-3-mentioned3", "translation": "of the sea"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-3-mentioned4", "translation": "of the sea"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-346-3-mentioned5", "translation": "of the river"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-comment1", "translation": "V. 905 suffers from confused construction, unless one writes ⟦1⟧ for ⟦2⟧ (the crasis of ⟦3⟧ is especially frequent, ⟦4⟧ 881 etc., ⟦5⟧). The emphasis lies on ⟦6⟧: not storms with dark sky and bad weather. Cf. ⟦7⟧ of Attica (⟦8⟧). After the ⟦9⟧ has thus been carried out at once, the ⟦10⟧ is returned to, and there follow the three items usually combined (also in curses): fruits — herds — children. Cf. ⟦11⟧, ⟦12⟧ (herds not mentioned, but see 25 ff.), ⟦13⟧, Aeschin. 3, 111 (Weckl.), and e.g. the Cretan inscription DI 5058, 40 ff.: ⟦14⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned1", "translation": "the winds"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned2", "translation": "and winds"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned3", "translation": "the (neuter plural article)"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned4", "translation": "the good things"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned5", "translation": "in sunny weather"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned6", "translation": "moderate breezes of winds"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned7", "translation": "from the sky"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned8", "translation": "from the earth"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-347-1-mentioned9", "translation": "that there be enjoyment of children and that the land bear fruit and the flocks thrive"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-348-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is transferred by zeugma to the ⟦2⟧;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-348-1-mentioned1", "translation": "fruit, crop"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-348-1-mentioned2", "translation": "flocks, herds"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-349-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ 'abundantly', cf. ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧ Andr. 349."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-349-1-mentioned1", "translation": "flowing upon, abundant"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-349-1-mentioned2", "translation": "when wealth flows in"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-349-1-quote1", "translation": "streams of evils"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-350-1-comment1", "translation": "V. 909 in ⟦1⟧ the object of ⟦2⟧ emerges again. 911"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-350-1-mentioned1", "translation": "salvation, deliverance"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-350-1-mentioned2", "translation": "to sing in praise"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-351-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧: while you protect the offspring (909), you may rather proceed in the opposite way against ⟦2⟧ (comparative with a kind of litotes, which has a threatening effect by virtue of the hint); ⟦3⟧ to carry out, as the gardener does the weeds."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-351-1-mentioned1", "translation": "more carrying out"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-351-1-mentioned2", "translation": "the impious"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-351-1-mentioned3", "translation": "to carry out"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-352-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ naturally only here;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-352-1-mentioned1", "translation": "may I produce"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-353-1-comment1", "translation": "912 ⟦1⟧ reference to the citizens present. Cf. ⟦2⟧ ⟦3⟧ — ⟦4⟧ (fictitious speech of Leucon). V. 913"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-353-1-mentioned1", "translation": "of these just men"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-353-1-mentioned2", "translation": "for some of the Athenians are perhaps worthless"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-353-1-mentioned3", "translation": "but considering the people good"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-354-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ = ⟦2⟧, you have as your office (others ⟦3⟧; but that would be ⟦4⟧)."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-354-1-mentioned1", "translation": "it is yours"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-354-1-mentioned2", "translation": "it is to you"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-354-1-mentioned3", "translation": "it is of you"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-354-1-mentioned4", "translation": "it is yours"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-355-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ in Aeschylus is nothing but ⟦2⟧, with the second part no longer felt, ⟦3⟧ ⟦4⟧, explained by Hesychius with ⟦5⟧, ⟦6⟧."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-355-1-mentioned1", "translation": "slain by Ares, warlike"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-355-1-mentioned2", "translation": "warlike, martial"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-355-1-mentioned3", "translation": "warlike spirit"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-355-1-mentioned4", "translation": "strong"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-355-1-mentioned5", "translation": "instead of 'like Ares'"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-356-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ also ⟦2⟧; ⟦3⟧ as 37 ⟦4⟧, and ⟦5⟧ 777;"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-356-1-mentioned1", "translation": "conspicuous, distinguished"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-356-1-mentioned2", "translation": "a city victorious in contests"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-356-1-mentioned3", "translation": "with swiftness of feet"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-356-1-mentioned4", "translation": "victorious with the spear"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-357-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ predicative."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-357-1-mentioned1", "translation": "victorious in the city"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-358-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ is forcefully said, as the whole thought is forceful and proud (on 864);"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-358-1-mentioned1", "translation": "I will not endure"}, {"id": "mvp-comment-359-1-comment1", "translation": "⟦1⟧ ⟦2⟧. 918."}, {"id": "mvp-comment-359-1-mentioned1", "translation": "the not"}]}